    <section class="doc-section">
      <div class="doc-container narrow">
        <h2>12 Answers Doctors Ask Us About Google Business Profile + Local SEO</h2>
        <p class="lede">Analysis based on ITD GrowthLabs' work across 20+ clinic engagements in India + GCC. Client names + case study details shared on discovery call under NDA.</p>

          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How important is Google Business Profile for a ENT + eye clinic?</h3>
            <div>Critical. 60-80% of new patient discovery for ENT and eye specialist practices in Mumbai starts with a Google search (e.g., 'ENT + eye near me' or 'ENT + eye in [area]'). Google's Map Pack (top-3 local results) captures 40-70% of clicks. Without an optimized Google Business Profile, you're invisible for the most valuable searches. GBP optimization is standard in every ITD tier including Starter.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How do you rank in the top-3 Map Pack for ENT + eye?</h3>
            <div>Ranking factors for ENT + Eye Specialists Map Pack (weighted): (1) Google Business Profile completeness + categories + services + Q&A — 25%, (2) Google review count + velocity + freshness — 25%, (3) proximity to searcher + business address quality — 20%, (4) NAP citation consistency across web — 15%, (5) website domain authority + local schema — 10%, (6) GBP posts + photos velocity — 5%. Sustained work across all six = top-3 within 6-9 months for most cities.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How many Google reviews does a ENT + eye clinic need?</h3>
            <div>Competitive benchmarks for Mumbai ENT and eye specialist practices: 20-50 reviews = viable but weak; 50-150 = competitive; 150-400 = top-tier; 400+ = category leader. What matters more than count: (1) recency (reviews in last 60 days), (2) 4.6+ average rating, (3) response rate 90%+, (4) keyword-rich reviews mentioning ENT specialist, ophthalmologist, LASIK, cataract, hearing aid, audiology, oculoplasty. ITD Growth+ tier includes review generation programme targeting 3-10 new reviews/month.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How does ITD generate Google reviews for ENT + eye clinics?</h3>
            <div>Post-visit review workflow: (1) WhatsApp follow-up 24 hours after visit, (2) SMS + email with direct Google review link, (3) NFC card at front desk for immediate review, (4) QR code on billing receipts, (5) monthly review incentive draw (compliance-safe — no review-quality incentive, just participation), (6) staff training on natural post-visit ask. Legit + compliant only — never fake or paid reviews (Google-suspend risk).</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>What GBP categories should a ENT + eye clinic use?</h3>
            <div>Primary category matters most (60% of category-based ranking signal). For ENT + Eye Specialists, use most-specific primary matching your practice: (1) Dermatologist / Dental clinic / Fertility physician / Orthopedic surgeon / etc. Add 4-8 secondary categories covering all services + specialties. Add all relevant service attributes + service areas. Update quarterly as Google adds new categories.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How often should a ENT + eye clinic post on Google Business Profile?</h3>
            <div>Recommended cadence: 2-4 GBP posts/week. Content mix: (1) offer + promotion posts — 30%, (2) event + patient education — 25%, (3) new-service or facility update — 20%, (4) before-after or team spotlight (compliance-safe) — 15%, (5) community + local news — 10%. Regular GBP posts boost Map Pack visibility 15-30% + drive direct calls.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>What NAP citation sources matter for ENT + eye?</h3>
            <div>Top NAP citation sources for ENT + Eye Specialists in Mumbai: (1) Practo, (2) Justdial, (3) Lybrate, (4) Sulekha, (5) Google Maps + Apple Maps + Bing Places, (6) 4-8 specialty directories per specialty (e.g., DentalPlanner, IVFClinicMumbai), (7) Facebook + Instagram business pages, (8) LinkedIn company page, (9) YouTube channel about, (10) local chamber-of-commerce + medical association directories. Consistency across 30-50 citations = ranking boost.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How do photos on Google Business Profile impact ranking?</h3>
            <div>GBP with 100+ photos ranks 2-3x higher in Map Pack than those with <20. Photo mix for ENT and eye specialist practices: (1) exterior + interior + reception + procedure rooms — 30%, (2) doctor + team + credentials + awards — 20%, (3) equipment + technology — 15%, (4) before-after (compliance-safe) — 15%, (5) patient events + community — 10%, (6) 360-degree virtual tour — 10%. Add 20-40 photos/month for velocity signal.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How do we optimize Google Q&amp;A for a ENT + eye clinic?</h3>
            <div>GBP Q&A is often overlooked but high-ROI. Best practice: (1) seed 20-40 owner-answered questions covering common patient concerns (ENT specialist, ophthalmologist, LASIK, cataract, hearing aid, audiology, oculoplasty), (2) monitor for user-asked questions daily + reply within 24 hours, (3) upvote high-quality user replies (boosts them), (4) include keywords + service categories naturally, (5) direct to booking link or WhatsApp for further discussion. Q&A visibility drives 10-20% of GBP profile-to-inquiry conversion.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How do you handle a negative review for a ENT + eye clinic?</h3>
            <div>ITD's negative review response protocol: (1) respond within 24 hours (delayed response signals lack of care), (2) empathetic + specific opener acknowledging concern, (3) request offline conversation (WhatsApp / phone / email — NEVER discuss medical details publicly), (4) close review with commitment to follow up, (5) internal ops review to prevent recurrence, (6) 30-day check-in to earn re-review if issue resolved. Never dispute or delete — Google penalizes.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How long before GBP optimization drives more patients?</h3>
            <div>Typical GBP optimization timeline for ENT and eye specialist practices: Week 1-2 = full profile completion + first 20 posts + photo backfill. Week 3-6 = review generation programme + Q&A seeding + citation audit. Week 7-12 = citation building + Map Pack ranking improvement (typically move up 3-8 positions). Month 4-6 = top-5 Map Pack achievable for less competitive cities/specialties, top-3 target month 6-12.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>Can ITD manage GBP for a multi-location ENT + eye chain?</h3>
            <div>Yes — Premium + Enterprise tier support multi-location GBP. Setup: (1) Google Business Profile Manager with per-location access + roles, (2) per-location content calendar + posts + photos, (3) centralized review response + escalation, (4) per-location Q&A + citations + ranking tracking, (5) monthly per-location performance report, (6) location-specific offer campaigns. Standard: 1-30 locations at Premium, 30+ at Enterprise.</div>
